OL,3,GNEWSASchool leaders vote in favour of
OL,4,Aindustrial action, says union
OL,5,
OL,6,FSchool leaders across Wales have voted
OL,7,Fin favour of industrial action over pay
OL,8,Fand additional learning needs (ALN)
OL,9,Ffunding, the trade union for
OL,10,Fheadteachers has announced.
OL,12,FNAHT Cymru, the Welsh branch of the
OL,13,FNational Association of Head Teachers,
OL,14,Fsaid the results from its statutory
OL,15,Fballot was a "clear and unmistakable
OL,16,Fmessage" about the growing pressures
OL,17,Ffacing schools and the profession.
OL,19,FIn a ballot with a 71% turnout, 95% of
OL,20,Fmembers voted in favour of industrial
OL,21,Faction short of a strike, while 71%
OL,22,Fwere in favour of strike action.
OL,23,APub: 27-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBWales NewsC Reg TVFClean Feed
FL,438,430,260,140,0,100
